      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I strongly advise against self-treating your eye with leftover antibiotic drops, as they can damage your cornea or disrupt your natural defenses if used unnecessarily. Using expired or improperly stored medication on an irritated eye could actually make an existing condition worse, such as a chemical burn or corneal abrasion. If the symptoms persist despite careful rinsing, you should see an eye doctor, even if it is costly, because vision loss can occur if a chemical injury or abrasion is ignored.",
